  "notes": "Drives two DC motors (or one stepper) from 5-35 V. Screw terminals along the +y edge, left to right: OUT1, OUT2 (motor A), +12V, GND, +5V, OUT3, OUT4 (motor B), 5.08 mm pitch, wires enter from +y. Header along the -y edge: ENA, IN1, IN2, IN3, IN4, ENB (2.54 mm). ENA/ENB to PWM pins (or leave the jumpers on for full speed), IN1-IN4 to digital pins; share GND with the board. With the 5V-EN jumper on and a supply of 12 V or less, the +5V terminal is an OUTPUT (about 5 V, 500 mA) that can power the Arduino; above 12 V remove the jumper.",
